+# Inductive Proof Guidance
+
+This document explains how to produce inductive/unbounded proofs for the safety invariants used by Aegis.
+
+Steps
+1. Identify invariants that should hold inductively (SafetyInvariant in TLA+ spec).
+2. For each invariant, attempt to show:
+   - Init => Invariant
+   - Invariant /\ Next => Invariant'
+3. Where needed, identify auxiliary lemmas and strengthen invariants until they become inductive.
+4. Use TLC to attempt unbounded checking (with symmetry and constraints) and produce a proof script.
+5. Record all TLC/Apalache traces and sign them (cosign) and register with Rekor.
+
+Mapping model->code
+- Produce docs/formal/proof_mapping.md that links each TLA+ variable and action to source files and line numbers (tools/policy_traceability.py provides a starting point).
+
+Deliverables for auditors
+- TLC/Apalache logs, proof artifacts, signed manifest of the runs, and mapping document.
